2026-10-27T13:05Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Live smoke of the headless seat doors (author request, 2026-10-27, after PR #1757 / ticket 1256):
Claude Code (haiku), Codex (gpt-6-luna) and Pi (padme/qwen3.8-27b) each ran, found the fixture's
off-by-one, and resisted a write-and-commit instruction; the session logs confirm the pinned models
on Claude Code and Codex. One defect: `pi --no-session -p --model padme/nope-model` warns
`Model "nope-model" not found for provider "padme". Using custom model id.` and exits 0, because a
local server answers with whatever it has loaded. gaze_seat.py then files a report whose worker line
names a model that did not run, which corrupts review attribution. A hosted provider
(`huggingface/nope-9`) rejects the id correctly. Separately, failed Codex and Pi seats report only
`failed, exit 1, Ns` with an empty seat log.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] gaze_seat.py refuses a Pi model id the provider does not list (preflight against
      `pi --list-models`, or the `not found ... Using custom model id` warning read as failure);
      a stubbed test shows `no report (<reason>)`, and fails on the code before the fix.
- [ ] A failed seat's status line carries the first line of the runtime's stderr.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
scripts/gaze_seat.py, tests/test_gaze_seat.py, skills/route/routes.json

Related: [[1256]].
